{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrR8re18RzjvA3duR1E3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the source of `AuthService.resetPassword`, so this diagnosis comes from the call graph and the report. It isn't confirmed against the code.\n\nThe graph shows `resetPassword` calling `getForgotSecret` (L401), `findById` (L384) and `usersService.update` (L415). It shows no call to anything in the session module, so nothing revokes the user's existing sessions. A phone that was already signed in keeps a valid session, and `refreshToken` keeps issuing new tokens for it. Refresh tokens are checked against the session, not the password.\n\n<br>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":66289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85b130be-8b08-4eec-bc5d-c100c9ce45ed","uuid":"8b08bc29-fb45-4a3c-aa56-96c8ba68e0d0","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:35:34.111Z","request_id":"req_011CgrR8rS7DiH1KfNjzW8Lm"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrR8re18RzjvA3duR1E3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AwtDKwUZiTjqCCg8BSfu15","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.resetPassword","start_line":367,"end_line":420,"explanation":"After verifying the reset hash and updating the password via usersService.update (around L415), the method does not invalidate the user's existing sessions. The call graph shows no call to the session service from resetPassword. Sessions on other devices therefore stay valid and can still use refreshToken to renew their login after a password reset."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.refreshToken","start_line":519,"end_line":545,"explanation":"Refresh only checks that the session still exists. Since resetPassword does not delete sessions, refresh keeps issuing new tokens for old devices. This is secondary: the root cause is the missing revocation in resetPassword."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.resetPassword, after the password is updated with usersService.update, delete all of the user's sessions, for example with `await this.sessionService.deleteByUserId({ userId: user.id })`. Inject SessionService into AuthService if it isn't already. Every device must then sign in again with the new password."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":66289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85b130be-8b08-4eec-bc5d-c100c9ce45ed","uuid":"6f1789f7-b869-4374-ae3d-0932